PATCH 449: mission WIN-DECLARATION -- a5dc 2da2 signedness + count/str-seg base-loss, + ba30 debrief
number-format base-loss.  ROOT: undefined2 is uint16_t, so a5dc's guard `if (DAT_2000_2da2 != -1)` is
`65535 != -1` = ALWAYS TRUE -> a5dc early-returns every frame and NEVER runs the side-count/win-check
(asm is `cmp word[2da2],0xffff; jne`).  Fixing a5dc's own guard (2da2/2da6 != 0xffff) makes the win-check
live; its count-path was ALSO base-lost (registry object read as host ptr at int*-stride 8; asm si=word
[DGROUP:bx], test byte[DGROUP:si+0x17], STRIDE 4) and its HUD write `es:[0x2d8e]=ax` dropped ES=word
[DGROUP:0x70] (str-seg) -> wild host write.  Rebased both.  ba30 (post-a814 debrief number formatter)
wrote its result into param_2 as a host pointer (callers pass DGROUP near offsets 0x432f..0x4399) ->
SIGSEGV; rebased param_2 to DGROUP.  RESULT: once the AI-vs-AI combat eliminates the enemy side (a296==0),
a5dc counts the side to 0 (max5790=16) and arms the mission-end (2da2=0x3c countdown -> DAT_2000_a814=0xff)
-> 459a returns via mission-end -> **the engine SELF-DECLARES the win (a814 fired)**.  NB the OTHER nine
`2da2 == -1` sites carry the same signedness bug but are left for now: fixing them opens a base-loss
cascade in the 2da2-gated flight-model code that stalls combat (board:0012, held/449 caveat) -- a5dc's
guard is fixed in isolation so the win-declaration works while the current (win-eliminating) combat
trajectory is preserved.  Post-resolution debrief screen (ba63 + siblings) still has its own base-loss
cascade (str-seg writes) -- separate follow-up.  ASM-verified vs re_out 0x1a5dc-0x1a664, 0x1ba30.
